# sourcePatchBlock: should a reload be blocked due to active source-patch state?
# Characterized from SourcePatchStateMachine.ReloadBlockReason (SourcePatchState.cs:62-73).
# C# stays native; this DSL + Python generated are the Python-side mirror.
# Output "blocked" = "source_patch_{state}_explicit_disable_required" (host interpolates state).
# Output "disableNotOwned" = "source_patch_disable_not_owned" (literal string).
# Output "allow" = no block (reload allowed; maps to null return in C# / '' in Python).
# First match wins; explicit-disable check must run before generic patch/lease/state check.
DECISION sourcePatchBlock DEFAULT allow
  disableOwned AT 10 WHEN patch.explicitOwnedDisable AND patch.state == Disabling AND patch.matchingDisableReceipt AND NOT patch.leaseHeld -> allow
  disableNotOwned AT 11 WHEN patch.explicitOwnedDisable -> disableNotOwned
  patchesActive AT 20 WHEN patch.patchesMayBeActive -> blocked
  leaseHeld AT 21 WHEN patch.leaseHeld -> blocked
  stateActive AT 22 WHEN NOT patch.stateIsOff AND NOT patch.stateIsUnavailable -> blocked
END
